# Part 11's control arm RUNS this program (panel 226's R1, 2026-10-20): the
# strict build refuses it under `ufcs_on_mutable`, a thesis rule, and the control arm,
# `build --permissive`, gives the dropped rule the meaning the sitting's
# table pins: `v.bump()` where `bump`'s first parameter is `@` lends `v`'s place, as `bump(@v)` does.
# The witness is the compiler-engineer's (w05-ufcs_on_mutable), one of 27 it ran before the
# resolution was written (`docs/panel/226-reports/compiler-engineer.md`).

function bump(@n: i64)
    n @ n + 1

function main()
    v: i64 @= 1
    v.bump()  #~ ufcs_on_mutable
    print(v)
